{
  "find": {
    "fullClassName": "topology.BgpRoutesNextHop",
    "filter": {
      "and": {
        "equal": [
          { "name": "routeTargetString", "value": "65000:10" },
          { "name": "nextHop", "value": "10.251.121.250" }
        ]
      }
    },
    "resultFilter": {
      "children": "",
      "attribute": [
        "objectFullName",
        "nextHop",
        "routeTargetString",
        "siteId"
      ]
    }
  }
}

Resultado real (PE 7705):
  tpgy-mgr:AS-65000:RT-65000%10:NH-10.251.121.250-Type-ipv4


================================================================
17) Habilitar grabacion BGP en el CPAA (NO es find)
================================================================
Que hace:
  configureInstance sobre topology.Cpaa. Agrega bit bgp a
  protocolRecord. Va a POST /v3/xml o /v3/request, no a /v3/find.
  Cambio de produccion: no ejecutar sin cambio autorizado.
  No alcanza para tener RIB si el 7701 no tiene sesion BGP VPNv4.

Body XML:
<generic.GenericObject.configureInstance xmlns="xmlapi_1.0">
  <deployer>immediate</deployer>
  <distinguishedName>network:10.251.243.250:cpaa</distinguishedName>
  <configInfo>
    <topology.Cpaa>
      <actionMask>
        <bit>modify</bit>
      </actionMask>
      <protocolEventTypes>
        <bit>ospf</bit>
        <bit>bgp</bit>
      </protocolEventTypes>
      <protocolRecord>
        <bit>ospf</bit>
        <bit>ospfTe</bit>
        <bit>bgp</bit>
      </protocolRecord>
      <administrativeState>up</administrativeState>
    </topology.Cpaa>
  </configInfo>
</generic.GenericObject.configureInstance>


================================================================
Mapa rapido: que query usar
================================================================
Servicio / cliente          →  1, 2, 3
Donde esta la VPRN          →  4, 5
Prefijo de SAP              →  6, 7
Estaticas                   →  8
Config BGP del VR           →  9
PEs de la VPN (RT)          →  15, 16
Prefijos BGP aprendidos     →  13, 14  (hoy vacio en este NFM-P)
Underlay OSPF               →  11  (siempre con children="")
Estado del recolector       →  10, 12

SAM-O no equivale a:
  show router 10 route-table
  show router 10 bgp routes
Eso queda en CLI del NE o en RIB CPAM cuando BgpRibInfo tenga datos.

